{"xson":[{"/iati-activities/iati-activity":[{"/activity-date":[{"@iso-date":"2008-12-17","@type":"2"},{"@iso-date":"2016-12-31","@type":"4"}],"/activity-status@code":"4","/collaboration-type@code":"2","/contact-info":[{"/organisation/narrative":[{"1":"International Fund for Agricultural Development","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"/person-name/narrative":[{"1":"Kasalu Coffin, Esther Chitila","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"/telephone":[{"1":"+390654591"}],"/website":[{"1":"http://www.ifad.org"}],"@type":"1"}],"/default-aid-type":[{"@code":"C01","@vocabulary":"1"}],"/default-tied-status@code":"5","/description":[{"/narrative":[{"1":"Key programme objectivesThe goal of the programme is to support improved and sustainable livelihoods of the rural poor, particularly women and vulnerable groups. The purpose is to improve the rural and agricultural population's access to sustainable financial services through enhanced outreach, sustainability and linkages, with a particular focus on smallholder farmers. Policy and institutional objectivesThe main institutional objective is to strengthen rural financial institutions and the linkages of smallholder farmers and other rural poor people to financial services, technical support and risk management instruments. The Programme will also contribute to developing a more enabling policy, regulatory and learning framework at the macro-level through the implementation of GHAMP and AFSAP. It will also strengthen meso-level institutions, such as the Ghana Micro-finance Network (GHAMFIN) and the Apex bank of RCBs.","@xml:lang":"EN"}]}],"/document-link":[{"/category":[{"@code":"A12"}],"/description/narrative":[{"1":"More information on how IFAD publish IATI data to ensure the effectiveness of development.","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"/language":[{"@code":"EN"}],"/title/narrative":[{"1":"IATI documentation on IFAD corporate website","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"@format":"TEXT/HTML","@url":"/en/iati"},{"/category":[{"@code":"A12"}],"/description/narrative":[{"1":"The IFAD website i